<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asia Minor</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> Minor is the historical name for the Anatolian peninsula, the western part of Asia corresponding to most of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. After the Seljuk victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-manzikert">Manzikert</a> in 1071, Turkish groups conquered and settled much of it. It became the base from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> arose at the end of the thirteenth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asia-minor.jpg" alt="Asia Minor" width="320" height="150" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Golden · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_geographic_region_of_Anatolia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
